ythms such as footwork, his productions exude funk, a veritable mishmash of styles that have always stayed true to style and shied far away from standardisation.\" (words by Lorna Smith of Inflect Bristol)\r\n\r\nFatGyver is Fanu's hip hop alter ego paying homage to the 90s US east coast style hip hop.\r\nFanu is also a mixing and mastering engineer, mostly working with bass music, hip hop, and related styles.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:168523","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":219674,"name":"Samurai (2)"},{"id":337198,"name":"FanuSamurai"},{"id":670955,"name":"Janne Hatula"},{"id":4273780,"name":"FatGyver"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Fansu","Janne Hatula (Fanu/FatGyver)"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/168523-Fanu","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/FanuMusic","https://soundcloud.com/FanuFatGyver","http://www.fanumusic.com","https://twitter.com/FanuFatGyver","https://instagram.com/FanuFatGyver","https://fanu.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/24204/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"24204","image":"https://i.discogs.com/nLcY_jtLBVxFANNk_S9FvrSFUhXUZvjAvn6zF0fbWXQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:313/w:455/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI0MjA0/LTE0NjMxMTQ4NjIt/NjAzMC5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/_P6nmMU9UqlFt13DoGqqmgvz-rR6H4WPPHvEwsjd1ys/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI0MjA0/LTE0NjMxMTQ4NjIt/NjAzMC5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Lootpack is a hip-hop trio from Oxnard, California, known for their jazz-influenced beats and intricate lyricism. The group consists of [a=Madlib] ([a=Otis Jackson Jr.]), [a=Wildchild (2)] ([a=Jack Brown (3)]), and [a=DJ Romes] ([a=Romeo Jimenez]). Producer [a=Kan Kick] was also an early member before pursuing a solo career. Lootpack first gained attention in the mid-1990s, making their debut on [a=Tha Alkaholiks]' Coast II Coast album in 1995. Their breakthrough came with the release of their 1999 debut album Soundpieces: Da Antidote! on [l=Stones Throw Records], a project that showcased Madlib’s signature off-kilter production and the group’s unique chemistry. While Lootpack never released another full-length album, its members remained highly active. Madlib went on to become one of hip-hop’s most celebrated producers, working with artists like MF DOOM, J Dilla, and Freddie Gibbs. Wildchild and DJ Romes also pursued solo projects, maintaining the group’s underground legacy.\r\nLootpack is regarded as a key influence in the underground hip-hop scene, helping to establish [l=Stones Throw Records] as a major force in independent rap.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:24204","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":346740,"name":"Otis Jackson Jr."},{"active":true,"id":862548,"name":"Jack Brown (3)"},{"active":true,"id":1073966,"name":"Romeo Jimenez"}],"namevariations":["Loot Pack","The Loot Pack","The Lootpack"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/24204-Lootpack","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.stonesthrow.com/lootpack/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4198486/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4198486","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4198486","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":4158561,"name":"Vito Foccacio"},{"active":true,"id":4158581,"name":"Loota"},{"active":true,"id":6265757,"name":"Dinero (12)"},{"active":true,"id":6487240,"name":"Iray"}],"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4198486-Squash-Squad","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/5151900/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"5151900","image":"https://i.discogs.com/-FHhEEo_q3VrvNhZVzSOvqaRuOICP9q2d508R-hiDIE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:400/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTUxNTE5/MDAtMTYyNjgxNzk0/Mi00MDc5LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Fb6GRnQ91gqR7tQnICrjGOm0o